<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<bpmn:definitions xmlns:bpmn="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/MODEL" xmlns:bpmndi="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/DI" xmlns:dc="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DC" xmlns:di="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DI" id="Defs_L3_3_4_2" targetNamespace="https://teck.example/process-models/pillar-03">
  <bpmn:collaboration id="Collab_L3_3_4_2">
    <bpmn:participant id="Pool_L3_3_4_2" name="3.4.2 Assay &amp; Analysis" processRef="Process_L3_3_4_2"/>
  </bpmn:collaboration>
  <bpmn:process id="Process_L3_3_4_2" isExecutable="false">
    <bpmn:documentation>L1/L3 Process. Chemical analysis of prepared samples determines the grade (metal content) of each process stream. Two parallel analytical channels exist: (1) the primary laboratory (fire assay for Au, ICP-OES/MS or XRF for base metals) for shift composite, daily composite, and concentrate product samples; (2) on-stream analysis (OSA) using online XRF analyzers for real-time process control.</bpmn:documentation>
    <bpmn:laneSet id="LaneSet_L3_3_4_2">
      <bpmn:lane id="Lane_L3_3_4_2_lab" name="Laboratory Analyst / Chief Metallurgist">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Start_L3_3_4_2_s</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_L3_3_4_2_3_4_2_1</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_L3_3_4_2_3_4_2_3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Gw_L3_3_4_2_g</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_L3_3_4_2_n1</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_L3_3_4_2_n2</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>End_L3_3_4_2_e</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
      </bpmn:lane>
      <bpmn:lane id="Lane_L3_3_4_2_osa" name="DCS (OSA integration) / Metallurgist">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Start_L3_3_4_2_s2</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Service_L3_3_4_2_3_4_2_2</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>End_L3_3_4_2_e2</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
      </bpmn:lane>
    </bpmn:laneSet>
    <bpmn:startEvent id="Start_L3_3_4_2_s" name="Assay pulps received">
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_L3_3_4_2_1</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:startEvent>
    <bpmn:task id="Task_L3_3_4_2_3_4_2_1" name="3.4.2.1 Perform Laboratory Assay">
      <bpmn:documentation>Primary laboratory analysis of prepared assay pulps using: ICP-OES or ICP-MS (for Cu, Zn, Pb, Fe, Mo, and trace elements), XRF (for major element oxides and base metals), or fire assay (for Au, Ag). Results are entered into LIMS with certified reference material results and QC flags. Laboratory TAT is typically 8–24 hours for routine shift composites; 24–48 hours for monthly certification samples. [P754: grade (Cu%, Zn%, Pb%, Ag g/t, Au g/t, Fe%, S%, Mo% where applicable, moisture %) | ICP-OES/ICP-MS, XRF, fire assay | per batch (shift composite, daily composite, certification sample) | Principles 1, 5, 6, 7, 8 | YES for concentrate certification samples; NO for intermediate stream composites]
ISA-95 level: 3
Actors: Laboratory Analyst
Standard alignment: ISA-95 Level 3; AMIRA P754 Principles 1, 5, 6, 7, 8
DDVC layer: Raw; Curated (assay_result)</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_L3_3_4_2_1</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_L3_3_4_2_6</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_L3_3_4_2_2</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:task>
    <bpmn:task id="Task_L3_3_4_2_3_4_2_3" name="3.4.2.3 Perform QA/QC on Analytical Results">
      <bpmn:documentation>The laboratory inserts QC samples at a defined rate: certified reference materials (CRMs — typically 1 in 10 samples), field duplicates (1 in 20 samples), and blanks (1 in 20 samples). LIMS compiles QC statistics: CRM accuracy (recovery %), duplicate precision (RPD %), blank contamination. Control charts (Shewhart or CUSUM) flag systematic bias. QA/QC failure triggers re-assay of the affected batch. [P754: bias detection and accuracy | QC statistical analysis in LIMS | per analytical batch | Principles 8, 10 | YES for concentrate certification — failure to meet QC criteria invalidates the associated commercial assay]
ISA-95 level: 3
Actors: Laboratory Analyst; Chief Metallurgist
Standard alignment: ISA-95 Level 3 (quality management); AMIRA P754 Principles 8, 10
DDVC layer: Raw; Curated (qc_performance_record)</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_L3_3_4_2_2</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_L3_3_4_2_3</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:task>
    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="Gw_L3_3_4_2_g" name="QC batch accepted?" default="Flow_L3_3_4_2_5">
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_L3_3_4_2_3</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_L3_3_4_2_4</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_L3_3_4_2_5</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>
    <bpmn:task id="Task_L3_3_4_2_n1" name="Issue re-assay instruction; flag results; hold batch">
      <bpmn:documentation>Derived from the Process Flow Narratives section (not a row in the Process Decomposition).</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_L3_3_4_2_5</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_L3_3_4_2_6</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:task>
    <bpmn:task id="Task_L3_3_4_2_n2" name="Release results in LIMS">
      <bpmn:documentation>Derived from the Process Flow Narratives section (not a row in the Process Decomposition).</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_L3_3_4_2_4</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_L3_3_4_2_7</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:task>
    <bpmn:endEvent id="End_L3_3_4_2_e" name="Assay results released">
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_L3_3_4_2_7</bpmn:incoming>
    </bpmn:endEvent>
    <bpmn:startEvent id="Start_L3_3_4_2_s2" name="Plant streams flowing; OSA operational">
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_L3_3_4_2_8</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:startEvent>
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="Service_L3_3_4_2_3_4_2_2" name="3.4.2.2 Analyse Streams via On-Stream XRF">
      <bpmn:documentation>Online XRF analyzers (multi-stream) continuously analyse slurry streams at 2–4 minute scan intervals, providing near-real-time grade data for process control. Each analyzer handles multiple streams sequentially via a stream sequencer. OSA data is used by the metallurgist for flotation control adjustments (reagent dosage, froth depth, air rate). OSA data is secondary to lab assay for accounting purposes — it provides the high-frequency trend for process control, not the definitive grade for mass balance closure. [P754: grade (Cu%, Zn%, Pb%, Fe%) | online XRF | continuous (2–4 min per stream per scan cycle) | Principles 6, 7 | YES for monitoring; NO for primary accounting — lab assay is primary]
ISA-95 level: 1 / 2
Actors: DCS (OSA data integration); Metallurgist
Standard alignment: ISA-95 Levels 1, 2; AMIRA P754 Principles 6, 7
DDVC layer: Raw (time-series: osa_grade_telemetry)</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_L3_3_4_2_8</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_L3_3_4_2_9</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:endEvent id="End_L3_3_4_2_e2" name="OSA data archived to PI Historian">
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_L3_3_4_2_9</bpmn:incoming>
    </bpmn:endEvent>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_L3_3_4_2_1" sourceRef="Start_L3_3_4_2_s" targetRef="Task_L3_3_4_2_3_4_2_1"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_L3_3_4_2_2" sourceRef="Task_L3_3_4_2_3_4_2_1" targetRef="Task_L3_3_4_2_3_4_2_3"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_L3_3_4_2_3" sourceRef="Task_L3_3_4_2_3_4_2_3" targetRef="Gw_L3_3_4_2_g"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_L3_3_4_2_4" name="Yes" sourceRef="Gw_L3_3_4_2_g" targetRef="Task_L3_3_4_2_n2"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_L3_3_4_2_5" name="No" sourceRef="Gw_L3_3_4_2_g" targetRef="Task_L3_3_4_2_n1"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_L3_3_4_2_6" sourceRef="Task_L3_3_4_2_n1" targetRef="Task_L3_3_4_2_3_4_2_1"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_L3_3_4_2_7" sourceRef="Task_L3_3_4_2_n2" targetRef="End_L3_3_4_2_e"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_L3_3_4_2_8" sourceRef="Start_L3_3_4_2_s2" targetRef="Service_L3_3_4_2_3_4_2_2"/>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_L3_3_4_2_9" sourceRef="Service_L3_3_4_2_3_4_2_2" targetRef="End_L3_3_4_2_e2"/>
  </bpmn:process>
  <bpmndi:BPMNDiagram id="Diagram_L3_3_4_2">
    <bpmndi:BPMNPlane id="Plane_L3_3_4_2" bpmnElement="Collab_L3_3_4_2">
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Pool_L3_3_4_2_di" bpmnElement="Pool_L3_3_4_2" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="20" y="20" width="1122" height="510"/></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Lane_L3_3_4_2_lab_di" bpmnElement="Lane_L3_3_4_2_lab" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="60" y="20" width="1082" height="340"/></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Lane_L3_3_4_2_osa_di" bpmnElement="Lane_L3_3_4_2_osa" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="60" y="360" width="1082" height="170"/></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Start_L3_3_4_2_s_di" bpmnElement="Start_L3_3_4_2_s"><dc:Bounds x="110" y="77" width="56" height="56"/><bpmndi:BPMNLabel><dc:Bounds x="88" y="139" width="100" height="28"/></bpmndi:BPMNLabel></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Task_L3_3_4_2_3_4_2_1_di" bpmnElement="Task_L3_3_4_2_3_4_2_1"><dc:Bounds x="202" y="65" width="170" height="80"/></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Task_L3_3_4_2_3_4_2_3_di" bpmnElement="Task_L3_3_4_2_3_4_2_3"><dc:Bounds x="408" y="65" width="170" height="80"/></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Gw_L3_3_4_2_g_di" bpmnElement="Gw_L3_3_4_2_g" isMarkerVisible="true"><dc:Bounds x="664" y="70" width="70" height="70"/><bpmndi:BPMNLabel><dc:Bounds x="649" y="36" width="100" height="28"/></bpmndi:BPMNLabel></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Task_L3_3_4_2_n1_di" bpmnElement="Task_L3_3_4_2_n1"><dc:Bounds x="614" y="235" width="170" height="80"/></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Task_L3_3_4_2_n2_di" bpmnElement="Task_L3_3_4_2_n2"><dc:Bounds x="820" y="65" width="170" height="80"/></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="End_L3_3_4_2_e_di" bpmnElement="End_L3_3_4_2_e"><dc:Bounds x="1026" y="77" width="56" height="56"/><bpmndi:BPMNLabel><dc:Bounds x="1004" y="139" width="100" height="42"/></bpmndi:BPMNLabel></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Start_L3_3_4_2_s2_di" bpmnElement="Start_L3_3_4_2_s2"><dc:Bounds x="110" y="417" width="56" height="56"/><bpmndi:BPMNLabel><dc:Bounds x="88" y="479" width="100" height="56"/></bpmndi:BPMNLabel></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Service_L3_3_4_2_3_4_2_2_di" bpmnElement="Service_L3_3_4_2_3_4_2_2"><dc:Bounds x="202" y="405" width="170" height="80"/></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="End_L3_3_4_2_e2_di" bpmnElement="End_L3_3_4_2_e2"><dc:Bounds x="465" y="417" width="56" height="56"/><bpmndi:BPMNLabel><dc:Bounds x="443" y="479" width="100" height="42"/></bpmndi:BPMNLabel></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Flow_L3_3_4_2_1_di" bpmnElement="Flow_L3_3_4_2_1"><di:waypoint x="166" y="105"/><di:waypoint x="202" y="105"/></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Flow_L3_3_4_2_2_di" bpmnElement="Flow_L3_3_4_2_2"><di:waypoint x="372" y="105"/><di:waypoint x="408" y="105"/></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Flow_L3_3_4_2_3_di" bpmnElement="Flow_L3_3_4_2_3"><di:waypoint x="578" y="105"/><di:waypoint x="664" y="105"/></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Flow_L3_3_4_2_4_di" bpmnElement="Flow_L3_3_4_2_4"><di:waypoint x="734" y="105"/><di:waypoint x="820" y="105"/><bpmndi:BPMNLabel><dc:Bounds x="738" y="85" width="27" height="14"/></bpmndi:BPMNLabel></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Flow_L3_3_4_2_5_di" bpmnElement="Flow_L3_3_4_2_5"><di:waypoint x="699" y="140"/><di:waypoint x="699" y="235"/><bpmndi:BPMNLabel><dc:Bounds x="705" y="144" width="21" height="14"/></bpmndi:BPMNLabel></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Flow_L3_3_4_2_6_di" bpmnElement="Flow_L3_3_4_2_6"><di:waypoint x="614" y="275"/><di:waypoint x="287" y="275"/><di:waypoint x="287" y="145"/></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Flow_L3_3_4_2_7_di" bpmnElement="Flow_L3_3_4_2_7"><di:waypoint x="990" y="105"/><di:waypoint x="1026" y="105"/></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Flow_L3_3_4_2_8_di" bpmnElement="Flow_L3_3_4_2_8"><di:waypoint x="166" y="445"/><di:waypoint x="202" y="445"/></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="Flow_L3_3_4_2_9_di" bpmnElement="Flow_L3_3_4_2_9"><di:waypoint x="372" y="445"/><di:waypoint x="465" y="445"/></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
    </bpmndi:BPMNPlane>
  </bpmndi:BPMNDiagram>
</bpmn:definitions>
